{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-j1-reviewer-fable-44","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:eb93048bfef98eab102f","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description names landform_id as the independent-unit column and states each rock glacier was surveyed exactly once, with no landform appearing twice among the 25 rows.","observed_value":"25 rows, 25 distinct landforms, one survey each","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":6,"end_line":8,"quoted_text":"No\nlandform was resurveyed and none appears twice, so the file holds 25 rows and\n25 distinct landforms."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":10,"end_line":11,"quoted_text":"One row is: one rock glacier, surveyed once and summarised by a single mean creep velocity\nIndependent unit column: landform_id"}]},{"description":"By direct inspection of the input CSV, the 25 data rows carry landform_id values RG-01 through RG-25 with zero duplicates, so no independent unit contributes more than one row to the row-independent procedure.","observed_value":"25 unique landform_id values (RG-01..RG-25), 12 micaschist rows and 13 orthogneiss rows","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"landform_id,bedrock_class,crest_elevation_m,mean_slope_deg,creep_velocity_cm_yr\nRG-01,micaschist,2685,17.4,24.7"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":26,"end_line":26,"quoted_text":"RG-25,orthogneiss,2678,18.9,16.0"}]},{"description":"The workflow enforces uniqueness of the independent-unit column before computing any statistics, raising an error if any landform_id repeats; the Welch t-test therefore runs only on data guaranteed to have one row per unit.","observed_value":"uniqueness guard on landform_id precedes stats.ttest_ind","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":39,"end_line":41,"quoted_text":"ids = [row[UNIT_COL] for row in rows]\n    if len(set(ids)) != len(ids):\n        raise ValueError(\"landform_id must be unique: one row per landform\")"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":62,"end_line":62,"quoted_text":"result = stats.ttest_ind(x, y, equal_var=False)"}]},{"description":"The report's design section and selected result accurately claim one row per landform and 25 independent observations, matching the data.","observed_value":"reported n = 12 + 13 = 25 equals the number of distinct landforms","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":5,"end_line":7,"quoted_text":"Each row of `data/input.csv` is one rock glacier, surveyed once. No landform\ncontributes more than one row, so the 25 velocity values are 25 independent\nobservations."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":25,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Welch two-sided t-test: micaschist-hosted rock glaciers creep 8.00 cm/yr faster than orthogneiss-hosted ones (24.00 vs 16.00 cm/yr; t = 4.06, df = 19.8, p < 0.001, Cohen's d = 1.65), one row per landform."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"Searched for any sign that an independent unit enters the procedure repeatedly (duplicate landform_id values, resurveys, row expansion or replication in the workflow) and found none; the reported group sizes, means, SDs, and Welch statistics (n = 12 vs 13, 24.00 vs 16.00 cm/yr, SD 5.63 vs 4.01, t = 4.06, df = 19.8, p < 0.001, d = 1.65) all reproduce from the 25-row CSV under one-row-per-landform analysis, leaving no unexplained inflation of effective sample size.","observed_value":"hand recomputation from data/input.csv reproduces all reported statistics; no duplication mechanism exists in workflow/analysis.py","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":13,"end_line":14,"quoted_text":"| micaschist | 12 | 24.00 | 5.63 |\n| orthogneiss | 13 | 16.00 | 4.01 |"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":21,"end_line":23,"quoted_text":"Difference in means (micaschist - orthogneiss): 8.00 cm/yr\nt = 4.06, Welch-Satterthwaite df = 19.8, p < 0.001\nCohen's d (pooled SD) = 1.65"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":48,"end_line":52,"quoted_text":"def velocities(label):\n        return np.array(\n            [float(row[VALUE_COL]) for row in rows if row[GROUP_COL] == label],\n            dtype=float,\n        )"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by (1) scanning all 25 landform_id values in data/input.csv for duplicates (none: RG-01 through RG-25 each appear exactly once), (2) checking the workflow for any code path that could replicate rows or aggregate repeated surveys into the test (there is none; a guard raises ValueError on duplicate IDs before stats.ttest_ind is called), and (3) recomputing the group counts, means, standard deviations, Welch t statistic, Welch-Satterthwaite df, and Cohen's d by hand from the CSV. All recomputed values (n = 12/13, means 24.00/16.00, SD 5.63/4.01, t = 4.06, df = 19.8, d = 1.65, p < 0.001) match the report, so the selected result is consistent with exactly one entry per independent unit and the issue could not be demonstrated.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]}